@@ -218,7 +218,7 @@ Modbus RTU. Build flags: `ENABLE_SDM_METER`, `SDM_METER_SERIAL` (default `Serial
 transceiver must switch direction by itself. When the meter answers, `/status` reports its
 values: `amp`/`voltage` (L1), `power` (total), `amp2`, `amp3`, `voltage2`, `voltage3`,
 `phases` (phases above 1 A), `meter_import_kwh`, `meter_valid`, `meter_present`, `meter_errors`,
-`meter_type` and `meter_serial`, and the session energy is integrated from the measured total power.
+`meter_type` and `meter_format`, and the session energy is integrated from the measured total power.
 If the meter does not answer for 30 s (box sold without meter), `meter_present` turns `false`, the
 controller values are used and the meter is only probed once a minute.
 
@@ -228,9 +228,19 @@ float) and then with the native DTS4921 map; the first one that gives 100–300
 `meter_type` (`sdm630` or `dts4921`, `unknown` before the first success). A wrong map answers with
 valid frames but nonsense (an integer read as float is close to 0 V) or with a Modbus exception.
 If the meter does not answer three times in a row (timeout or bad CRC), the other parity is tried:
-8N1 and 8E1 (`meter_serial`). The DTS4921 ships with address 1, 9600 baud, 8E1. The last working
+8N1 and 8E1 (`meter_format`). The DTS4921 ships with address 1, 9600 baud, 8E1. The last working
 setting is tried first on the next detection. All values keep their units (V, A, W, kWh).
 
+On the Kinetos controller (firmware 8.x) the meter values are also fed to the controller, as the
+original firmware did: `$F2 0` switches it to external values, then `$T0 <mA L1> <mA L2> <mA L3>`
+follows every 2 s and `$T1 <Wh>` whenever the import energy changes, charging or not. If the
+controller refuses `$F2 0` (for example while it is disabled or still booting), it is retried
+every second six times and then every minute; it is repeated every 10 minutes and after a `$T0`
+answered with NK. `/status` shows `controller_meter_feed` (on/off), `controller_meter_feed_state`
+(`on`, `enabling`, `f2_rejected`, `f2_no_answer`, `t0_rejected`, `meter_invalid`,
+`controller_not_8x`), `controller_meter_feed_answer` (last RAPI result of `$F2 0`: 0 OK, 1 NK,
+-1 timeout) and `controller_firmware`.
+
 | Value | SDM630 (float) | DTS4921 (32 bit, high word first) |
 | --- | --- | --- |
 | Voltage L1-L3 | 0x0000/02/04 | 0x0100/02/04, uint32, 0.1 V |
